{"name":"Catfish","hex":"#657d82","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"catfish","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any fish of the order Siluriformes, mainly found in fresh water, lacking scales, and having barbels like whiskers around the mouth.","The meat of such a fish, popular in the Southern U.S. and Central Europe."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To fish for catfish."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/catfish"}],"entries":[{"title":"Catfish","blocks":[{"text":"Catfish are a diverse group of ray-finned fish of the order Siluriformes. Catfish are named for their prominent barbels, which resemble a cat's whiskers, though not all catfish have prominent barbels. All Siluriformes lack scales, instead possessing either smooth skin or armour-plated bodies. This order of fish are defined by features of the skull and swimbladder. Catfish range in size and behavior from the three largest species alive, the Mekong giant catfish from Southeast Asia, the wels catfish of Eurasia, and the piraíba of South America, to detritivorous and scavenging bottom feeders, down to the tiny ectoparasitic species known as the candiru."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Siluriformes.png/330px-Siluriformes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catfish","wikidata":"Q59576"},{"title":"Catfish (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Catfish is a 2010 American documentary film directed by Henry Joost and Ariel Schulman. It involves a young man, Nev, being filmed by his brother and friend, co-directors Ariel and Henry, as he builds a romantic relationship with a young woman on the social networking website Facebook. The film was a critical and commercial success. It led to an MTV reality TV series, Catfish: The TV Show. The film is credited with coining the term catfishing: a type of deceptive activity involving a person creating a fake social networking presence for nefarious purposes."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/7/73/Catfish_film.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Catfish_(film)","wikidata":"Q2915039"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/BARBEL_%28PSF%29.png/500px-BARBEL_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/BARBEL_%28PSF%29.png/500px-BARBEL_%28PSF%29.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABARBEL_(PSF).png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Channelcat.jpg/500px-Channelcat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/Channelcat.jpg/500px-Channelcat.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChannelcat.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg/500px-Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg/1280px-Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg/500px-Image-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A sting from the striped eel catfish, Plotosus lineatus, may be fatal. These are juveniles","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AImage-Striped_eel_catfish2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fd/Blue_